# Web-based bioinformatics tools

This study used several publicly available web-based bioinformatics platforms for taxonomic identification, antimicrobial resistance gene characterization, plasmid analysis, and in-silico serotyping.

## KmerFinder

- Platform: DTU Center for Genomic Epidemiology
- KmerFinder version: 3.2
- Software version: 3.0.2
- Database version: 2022-07-11
- Purpose: Species identification of successfully assembled genomes

## Pathogenwatch / Speciator

- Pathogenwatch version: 23.5.6
- Species identification pipeline: Speciator
- Purpose: Independent species identification of assembled genomes

## CARD / RGI

- RGI version: 6.0.5
- CARD database version: 4.0.1
- Input: Assembled genome FASTA
- Retained hits: Perfect and Strict
- Nudge hits excluded
- High quality/coverage option applied
- Minimum identity threshold: 100%
- Minimum coverage threshold: 60%

## ResFinder

- ResFinder version: 4.7.2
- Database version: 2.5.1
- Platform: DTU Center for Genomic Epidemiology
- Minimum identity threshold: 100%
- Minimum coverage threshold: 60%

## PlasmidFinder

- Web-tool version: 2.1
- Software version: 2.0.1 (2020-07-01)
- Database version: 2023-01-18
- Platform: DTU Center for Genomic Epidemiology
- Minimum identity threshold: 100%
- Minimum coverage threshold: 60%
- Applied to specimens with at least one detected AMR gene

## SerotypeFinder

- Web-tool version: 2.0
- Software version: 2.0.1 (2020-07-27)
- Database version: 1.0.0 (2022-05-16)
- Platform: DTU Center for Genomic Epidemiology
- Minimum identity threshold: 95%
- Minimum coverage threshold: 60%
- Purpose: In-silico serotyping of Escherichia coli isolates

## Galaxy Kraken2

- Galaxy platform version: 24.2
- Kraken2 version: 2.1.3
- Database: 2025-02-05T2046097_standard_prebuilt_core_nt_2024-0904
- Purpose: Taxonomic identification of assembled genomes
